								<TR>
									<TD style="COLOR: #000099; HEIGHT: 1px" vAlign="top" align="right" bgColor="#f5f5f5"><STRONG>DKP 
											FAQ</STRONG></TD>
								</TR>
								<TR>
									<TD style="COLOR: #000099" vAlign="top" align="left" bgColor="whitesmoke">
										<P style="COLOR: #000099" align="center">
											<TABLE id="Table2" style="HEIGHT: 308px" cellSpacing="1" cellPadding="1" width="587" border="0">
												<TR>
													<TD vAlign="top" align="left" bgColor="whitesmoke"><STRONG>What is DKP?</STRONG>
														<BR>
														<BR>
														DKP, short for dragon kill points. These points are awarded to each individual 
														as they attend a guild raid. The current DKP of each member reflects his or her 
														priority for loot. Essentially, the eligibility of a guild member for an item 
														based on raid attendance is now quantified by your DKP standing. When a member 
														wins an item, they lose a DKP amount that reflects the value of the item.
														<BR>
														<BR>
														<STRONG>How is positive DKP earned?</STRONG>
														<BR>
														<BR>
														Positive DKP is earned by attending raids and other major guild events. Each 
														event will have its own DKP value that will be assigned after the event takes 
														place. Some events will have more DKP than others based on the difficulty of 
														the event and the amount of time it takes to complete the event.
														<BR>
														<BR>
														<STRONG>Is DKP assigned per player or per character?</STRONG>
														<BR>
														<BR>
														DKP is per player.
														<BR>
														<BR>
														<STRONG>If I play than one character on a raid will I earn DKP for each?</STRONG>
														<BR>
														<BR>
														No.
														<BR>
														<BR>
														<STRONG>Who will track DKP?</STRONG>
														<BR>
														<BR>
														DKP is tracked by the officer that sponsors you into the guild or by the 
														officer in charge of attendance and loot at a particular raid. After an event, 
														the officer records the attendance of their members into the web database using 
														the DKP tool. Additionally, officers are responsible for tracking their own 
														DKP. If an officer knows that they cannot attend an event, they will have to 
														arrange for another officer to record their members' attendance.
														<BR>
														<BR>
														<STRONG>How can I tell how much DKP I have?</STRONG>
														<BR>
														<BR>
														By viewing the DKP database you will be able to see your current DKP as well as 
														how much DKP you have earned and how much you have spent. Use this link to 
														reference player DKP totals.
														<BR>
														<BR>
														<STRONG>How do I spend DKP?
															<BR>
														</STRONG>
														<BR>
														In a guild event or in a pick up group that an officer has determined that loot 
														will be awarded via DKP, if an item drops that you want, you can bid current 
														DKP to win that item. Bidding is done via "max bid". See the FAQ question on 
														"How do I bid?" for more information on this. How do I bid? When an item drops 
														that is eligible for DKP bidding, an officer will call for bids on that item. 
														The officer will additionally specify whether the bidding is "open" (meaning 
														you can bid on the item for an alt or for sale purposes) or if not specified 
														the bidding is for "mains only." The officer will call for max bids in 
														guildchat on the item 3 times. You need to send a tell to the officer in charge 
														of the bidding with the maximum amount you are willing to pay for that item in 
														DKP. If you have the high bid, you will win the item for 1 more DKP than the 
														second place bidder bid.
														<BR>
														<BR>
														For example: A moss snake drops a snake skin that Snaggle, Felong and Avid all 
														want. The officer in charge of loot calls in guildchat "Accepting max bids or 
														wishlist on "a snake skin", first call!
														<BR>
														<BR>
														Felong tells bid officer: bid 134
														<BR>
														Snaggle tells bid officer: bid 80
														<BR>
														Avid tells bid officer: bid 75
														<BR>
														<BR>
														The bid officer will make two more calls to make sure all bids are in for the 
														item before announcing the winner of the item (Felong for 81 dkp -- grats 
														Felong on new thong!).
														<BR>
														<BR>
														See the section on wishlist items for more information on that special 
														condition.
														<BR>
														<BR>
														<STRONG>Can I get an item for my secondary or tertiary character using DKP?</STRONG>
														<BR>
														<BR>
														Yes, but only if everyone else passes on bidding for that item or the loot 
														officer calls that the item is "open bid".
														<BR>
														<BR>
														<STRONG>When can I use DKP to get items for my secondary characters?</STRONG>
														<BR>
														<BR>
														Every three months you can switch your primary character out with a secondary 
														character. The new primary character is now the beneficiary of the DKP you 
														earn. One weeks notice must be given to your commanding officer before 
														switching primary characters.
														<BR>
														<BR>
														<STRONG>How does the "wish list" work?</STRONG>
														<BR>
														<BR>
														Your wishlist is "earned." New members do not have wishlist slots, rather they 
														are available every 100dkp earned to a maximum of 5 slots. As these slots open, 
														the member earning the slots is responsible for alerting the web monkey or 
														their reporting officer of what item they would like added to their wishlist -- 
														this can be ANY item in the game save for quest "end result" items or certain 
														Snaggle designated loot such as ST key pieces. If an item on your wish list 
														drops, you need to send a tell to the loot officer alerting them that the item 
														is on your wishlist. At this point, no DKP bidding will be allowed and you get 
														the item for the minimum required DKP for that item. If an item is on multiple 
														wishlists, then the player with the most earned dkp will get the item. In the 
														rare event that multiple people have the same dkp and the same item wishlisted 
														the item will be bid on using current dkp by ONLY those members via the max bid 
														system.
														<BR>
														<BR>
														<STRONG>How does a wish list slot get locked?
															<BR>
														</STRONG>
														<BR>
														Whenever you receive an item from your wishlist, the slot that corresponds to 
														that item becomes "locked". Locked slots may not be modified every two months 
														when you refresh your wish lists - only unlocked slots may be updated every two 
														months. Usually, locked slots will be reset a year's end, or at designated time 
														agreed upon by the officers. The idea for locking slots is to guarantee that no 
														one receives more than 5 wish list items over a set span of time (usually 1 
														year), but still allows flexibility in wish lists through allowing players to 
														modify their "unlocked" slots every two months.
														<BR>
														<BR>
														<STRONG>How many slots do I get for my wish list?</STRONG>
														<BR>
														<BR>
														Starting September 1, 2002, all existing members will retain whatever 
														"unlocked" slots they had previously. Locked slots will remain locked 
														indefinitely (at least through year's end). New members will start with no wish 
														list slots. Every 100dkp a new member earns will earn them 1 wishlist slot, 
														beginning with slot 5 and progressing through slot 1 (at 500dkp). On January 1, 
														2003, an improved system will be put in place that may or may not include wish 
														lists. It is likely that improved system will include lists in a more limited 
														capactity.
														<BR>
														<BR>
														<STRONG>How often will the DKP rules change?
															<BR>
														</STRONG>
														<BR>
														Every two months the officers will review the DKP rules and make changes based 
														on the members' feedback.
													</TD>
